\pard\plain\f0\sa160\sl276\slmult1\cf1\b\fs22 Application for On-the-Job Training (OJT)\par
\pard\plain\f0\sa200\sl276\slmult1\cf3\fs22 Dear Sir/Madam,\par
\pard\plain\f0\sa200\sl276\slmult1\cf3\fs22 I would like to apply for my On-the-Job Training (OJT) at the Filamer Christian University Library. I am a 4th-year Bachelor of Science in Information Technology student here at Filamer and I am expected to graduate in 2027. As a Filamer student myself, I know how important the library is to students and teachers and I would be glad to help in any way I can.\par
\pard\plain\f0\sa200\sl276\slmult1\cf3\fs22 In school, I have worked with Python, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and MySQL. For our capstone project, I am the lead frontend developer of an Emergency Response Community Platform for the Municipality of Jamindan, where I worked on the map and the emergency reporting page. Before that, I made the Quintic Laundry System, a web system for keeping track of orders, billing and customer records. Working on these projects taught me how to handle data carefully and how to make systems that are easy for people to use.\par
\pard\plain\f0\sa200\sl276\slmult1\cf3\fs22 I also had hands-on training in assembling computers, fixing hardware problems, installing operating systems and setting up a LAN. I think these can be useful in the library, whether it is encoding and organizing records, helping with the digital catalog, or checking the computers when something goes wrong.\par
\pard\plain\f0\sa200\sl276\slmult1\cf3\fs22 I know I still have a lot to learn, and I am excited to learn from the library staff. I am willing to do the tasks given to me, help library users, and follow the rules and procedures of the library.\par
\pard\plain\f0\sa200\sl276\slmult1\cf3\fs22 Thank you for taking the time to read my letter. I have attached my resume for your reference. I hope to have the chance to talk with you about my application.\par
\pard\plain\f0\sb120\sa600\sl276\slmult1\cf3\fs22 Sincerely yours,\par
\pard\plain\f0\sl276\slmult1\cf3\b\fs22\expndtw6 JHON STEVEN ALTOVEROS\par
